text:
sara: quick prototype drop — 'deep panel' dark mode for the dashboard. tightened syntax contrast and new sparkline palette. preview: https://invis.io/deep-panel-proto

matt: nice direction. two quick nits: inline code keywords feel low-contrast at 12px, and the sparklines disappear against the panel when there’s a dense background grid.

aliya: agree with matt on keywords. also watch for red/green distinction in sparkline series — we should pick colors that pass colorblind checks.

jordan: sketched a modest tweak — raise keyword luminance ~12% and add a subtle 1px outer blur for small code tokens so they pop without looking haloed. also increased sparkline stroke from 1 to 1.5 on hover.

samir: a11y checklist: headings >= 4.5:1 vs background for small headings; body copy >= 4.5:1; inline code/badges >= 3:1 minimum. For tokens in code blocks we can accept 3:1 if we compensate with weight or bg chip.

matt: for charts — prefer using saturated but darker accents (avoid neon brights). suggestion: use these token names instead of raw hexs so designers/devs reuse them: `--spark-accent-1`, `--spark-accent-2`, `--spark-muted`, `--panel-deep-bg`.

jordan: quick CSS example I tried:

```css
:root {
  --panel-deep-bg: #0b0f12; /* deep, not pure black */
  --syntax-default: #d6e6ff;
  --syntax-keyword: #a6d2ff; /* bumped luminance */
  --syntax-fn: #ffd6a6;
  --spark-accent-1: #6bd4b0;
  --spark-accent-2: #7aa6ff;
  --spark-muted: rgba(255,255,255,0.08);
}
.code-inline { color: var(--syntax-default); }
.code-inline .kw { color: var(--syntax-keyword); text-shadow: 0 0 1px rgba(0,0,0,0.4); }
.sparkline { stroke-width: 1; stroke-linecap: round; }
.sparkline:hover { stroke-width: 1.5; }
```

sara: that looks promising. can we add a variant for high-contrast toggle that maps `--syntax-keyword` -> `#cfe6ff` and `--spark-muted` -> rgba(255,255,255,0.14)?

aliya: yes — also test with simulators for deutan/protan. i can run a quick pass and push suggestions.

samir: minor copy nit: in the metrics panel the toggle says `Show token history` — suggest `Usage history` (shorter + less jargon).

matt: charts UX nit — when a sparkline is very flat we should add micro-guides (light dotted baseline) so slope is visible on deep backgrounds. baseline should be 6% lighter than panel bg.

sara: good call. copy tweak noted. also adding a tiny hover focus for sparklines: 2px outer glow at 12% opacity of accent to meet focus visibility.

devops-bot: preview deploy ready at https://staging.redwood/preview/deep-panel-1934 — screenshot attached :thumbsup:

aliya: testing now in Lighthouse + axe. will post results in thread (quick pass looks like keyword contrast still borderline at 12px).

jordan: i'll iterate token hues and push to branch `design/deep-panel-sparkline` — will include a colorblind-safe palette and a11y token mapping.

sara: thanks all — I'll open PR with the copy changes and link the accessibility checklist. landing goal: get axe-green and colorblind pass before we flip to default dark.

matt: thumbs up. small follow-up: can we keep an optional bg texture off by default? it adds noise and dims sparklines on small screens.

sara: noted. we'll make it an opt-in `--panel-bg-texture: none | subtle-grid`.

jordan: leaving a final comment: aim for consistent token roles (keywords, functions, strings) across all panels so devs see the same semantics in mini-code everywhere.

sara: perfect — thanks everyone, moving into design QA.
